{"id":"u-ac7c1829-0a1c-415d-a174-6afa9362b96e","src":"community","title":"NO COMPROMISE - GZCL/CALI","author":"Jackson H.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/RYDWR3-gzclcali","desc":"[[WORK IN PROGRESS]]\n\nHybrid GZLP/Calisthenics programme to effectively build strength, muscle and cali skills.\n\nAfter running GZLP for 6 months with great results then 6 months of pure calisthenics I have decided to try and cross-programme the two. \nThis programme also takes partial inspiration from the athlete oriented High-Low ethos of programming.\n\nThe core difference to standard GZLP is that OHP has been swapped for Pull-ups (Weighted) (for the 4 sets of 3-5 format) and Bodyweight Pullups (for the 3 sets of 10 format) to emphasise more calisthenics oriented pulling.\nFurthermore, the supplementary T3 exercises (Lat Pull-down and Bent over Rows) have been swapped for EZY bar Curls and OHP.\n\nTier 1: A primary compound lift (Squat, RDL, Pull-up, Bench) done for 5 sets of 3 reps\nTier 2: A secondary compound lift done for 3 sets of 10 reps\nTier 3: Accessory exercises (Curls, OHP) done for 3 sets of 10-15 reps at light weight \n\nWhen to add weight?\nFor T1 and T2 add:\n- 2.5/5kg every workout until set failure. \n- Then keep weight and change to either (6x2 for T1) or (3x8 for T2)\nFor T3 add:\n- If you can do 20-25 reps add weight\n- If you fail lower weight by 15% and try again\n\nCore Values\n- Legs get hit everyday.\n- Power, speed and hypertrophy are all equally important.\n- Day 5 is light aerobic work with mobility work or HIIT, conditioning\n- No workout is longer than 1-1.5hrs max.\n- Consistency over intensity.\n- Switch is up. Keep it fun. Consistency will follow.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Athletics","Strength","Bodyweight Fitness"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-14T15:01:31.553Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5","Day 6","Day 7"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3},{"r":10}]},{"n":"Pistol Squat","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Archer Pushups","sets":[{"r":20,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"HIIT/RUN","sets":[{"sec":3600}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":5,"x":3},{"r":8}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2},{"r":20}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2},{"r":20}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3},{"r":10}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Box Jump","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"HIIT/RUN","sets":[{"sec":0}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Planche","sets":[{"sec":60,"x":4}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Light Jog","sets":[{"sec":1800}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3},{"r":10}]},{"n":"Pistol Squat","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Archer Pushups","sets":[{"r":20,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"HIIT/RUN","sets":[{"sec":3600}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":5,"x":3},{"r":8}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2},{"r":20}]},{"n":"Hip Thrust (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":2},{"r":20}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"x":3},{"r":5}]},{"n":"Squat (